8. Page 5 — Opportunity Scoring

Create a transparent weighted scoring system.

Use exactly these initial weights:

Criterion| Weight
People affected| 20%
Pain / severity| 20%
Willingness to pay| 25%
Market potential| 15%
Competition / gap| 10%
Feasibility| 10%

Every criterion is scored from 1–10.

Calculate:

Business Score =
(People × 20%)
+ (Pain × 20%)
+ (WTP × 25%)
+ (Market × 15%)
+ (Gap × 10%)
+ (Feasibility × 10%)

Normalize the final result to 0–100.

Display:

85–100

Exceptional Opportunity

70–84

Strong Opportunity

55–69

Needs Validation

40–54

Weak Opportunity

Below 40

Low Priority

Make the score completely transparent.

Users must be able to change every score manually.

---

9. Human-in-the-loop principle

Never allow the AI score to become the final truth.

Example:

AI suggests:

«Willingness to pay: 8/10»

Human research shows:

«Only 1 of 20 people would pay.»

The user must be able to change it to:

«3/10»

The final score should immediately update.

Show:

«AI hypothesis

Human-adjusted score

Evidence strength»

This is a core product feature.

